  "id": "BIT-postgresql-2026-116325",
  "summary": "PostgreSQL reindexdb index name quoting allows SQL injection",
  "details": "SQL injection in PostgreSQL reindexdb allows an object creator to execute arbitrary SQL as the database user running reindexdb, via a crafted index name embedded in the parallel catalog query for --jobs with --index.  Within major versions 17-18, minor versions before PostgreSQL 18.7 and 17.12 are affected.  Versions before PostgreSQL 17 are unaffected.",
